model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Combining selected account sources preserves each source's error without making a healthy source unusable. Catalog diagnostics identify failed accounts separately from healthy tools. Provider-error coverage checks partial MCP catalogs and indexes, exact safe diagnostic fields, selected-account failures, successful retries and rediscovery after reconnecting the same account. Calls retain account selection, credential redaction, cancellation and approval authority; a selected failed source returns its own failure. For this upstream sync, partial listings stay fresh until their inputs or credential generation change; reconnect invalidates them and permits rediscovery. Retrying discovery on the next read is a separate follow-up requiring independent qualification. Single-source failures remain failures. Selected tool execution preserves account traffic attribution before its handler and validation. The four source-isolation scenarios stay scheduled and selected in their owned account job. Embedded MCP Apps assets are regenerated with the same carried runtime and pinned Bun compiler."
    }
  }
}
